Whom to ask first was decided by labels and relationship strength only. A
wave's remaining people are now ordered:
  1. the person the goal's own text names (D625);
  2. the pre-match class of 1694 — likely_yes, possibly, ask_him, and
     not_his_field only when nobody else is left;
  3. within a class, the answer rate in this field, (yes + referred + 1) /
     (asked + 2), then the overall rate, from 1689's answer_stats;
  4. then the plan's order.
The two signals stay two numbers on their own records; nothing merged is
stored. A failed read keeps the plan's order. The bridge choice (A14) is not
built yet and will use the same order.

DONE WHEN: four fictional candidates with known records come out in the
defined order; changing one record changes the order as expected; the
owner-named person is always first.

